-## 9. Code Examples (libcurl, POSIX)
+## 9. Gateway Configuration
+
+Runtime gateway settings are read from `config/gateway.conf` when the gateway starts.
+The rate limiter supports these keys:
+
+```conf
+rate_limit_enabled = true;
+rate_limit_requests = 100;
+rate_limit_window_seconds = 60;
+```
+
+| Key | Type | Description |
+|-----|------|-------------|
+| `rate_limit_enabled` | boolean | Enables or disables global per-IP request throttling. Use `true` or `false`. |
+| `rate_limit_requests` | integer | Number of requests allowed per client IP in one window. |
+| `rate_limit_window_seconds` | integer | Window size, in seconds, used for the request quota. |
+
+With the sample values above, each client IP can make 100 requests every 60 seconds.
+Excess requests receive HTTP `429` with `{ "error": "Rate limit exceeded" }`.
+Set `rate_limit_enabled = false;` to disable throttling.
+
+---
